\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Local boundary portraits for $\kappa >0$, after a positive time rescaling setting $k=1$. In $U_2$ and $V_2$, moving trajectories run parallel to the red equilibrium line. In $U_3$ and $V_3$, they form outgoing and incoming rays at $p_f^+$ and $p_f^-$, respectively. Every point on a red line is stationary. For $\kappa <0$, all blue arrows reverse.}}{22}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:local-infinity}{{2}{22}{Local boundary portraits for $\kappa >0$, after a positive time rescaling setting $k=1$. In $U_2$ and $V_2$, moving trajectories run parallel to the red equilibrium line. In $U_3$ and $V_3$, they form outgoing and incoming rays at $p_f^+$ and $p_f^-$, respectively. Every point on a red line is stationary. For $\kappa <0$, all blue arrows reverse}{figure.2}{}}
